		"innerColor": [163, 8, 34],

        "startIntroPart1": "History remembers revolutions by the promises they make. The Crimson Imperium remembers the one that kept its promise: the revolution led by Yuri Volkov. He overthrew a monarchy that had mistaken its ancient privileges for an eternal right to rule. The people stood beside him, believing that a new age had begun. And a new age did begin. The old symbols were torn down, the institutions of the crown were dismantled, and a fractured nation was forged into a single state. Yet freedom alone cannot build a country, and hope alone cannot defend it. Today, the Volkar live beneath the crimson banner of an empire built on discipline, sacrifice, and unbreakable unity. Some remember the revolution with pride. Others remember what followed with fear. Yuri Volkov remembers both, and he has no intention of allowing history to repeat itself.",
        "startIntroPart2": "Yuri Volkov, First Leader of the Crimson Imperium, the architect of a revolution and guardian of a nation that cannot afford another collapse. Your people look to you for direction, whether through conviction or necessity. Beyond your borders lie rivals who would exploit every weakness, while within them linger those who dream of restoring the old order. You know what disorder costs. You know how quickly a nation can be brought to its knees when its people lose faith in its institutions. The Volkar do not need another king, nor do they need another revolution. They need a future that cannot be taken from them. Will you secure the borders, strengthen the state, and prove that the Crimson Imperium can endure long after its enemies have vanished? History will judge your methods. Your people will live with their consequences. The choice is yours, Yuri Volkov."
	    "declaringWar": "You mistook our restraint for weakness; now you will learn the price of that mistake.",
